{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PHhS9sphifHNogcY1QTcSZ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: srd053-logname\n2\ttitle: \"cmd/logname: Print Login Name\"\n3\t\n4\tproblem: |\n5\t  The logname utility prints the login name of the current user as recorded by the system\n6\t  login process. Unlike whoami (which reports the effective username), logname reports the\n7\t  original login identity, which may differ after su or sudo. The Go implementation must\n8\t  match the Homebrew GNU reference binary (glogname, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte\n9\t  on stdout and exit code, verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n10\t\n11\tgoals:\n12\t  - G1: Print the login name of the current user followed by a newline.\n13\t  - G2: Reject any extra operands with an error message and nonzero exit.\n14\t\n15\trequirements:\n16\t  R1:\n17\t    title: Default behavior\n18\t    items:\n19\t      - R1.1:\n20\t          text: When invoked with no arguments, must print the login name followed by a newline and exit 0.\n21\t      - R1.2:\n22\t          text: The login name must be obtained from the system login record (getlogin(3) or equivalent), not from the effective UID.\n23\t\n24\t  R2:\n25\t    title: Error handling\n26\t    items:\n27\t      - R2.1:\n28\t          text: If any extra operand is provided (beyond --help and --version), must print an error message to stderr and exit 1.\n29\t      - R2.2:\n30\t          text: Unknown flags must produce an error message to stderr and exit 1.\n31\t      - R2.3:\n32\t          text: If the login name cannot be determined (e.g., no controlling terminal), must print an error to stderr and exit 1.\n33\t\n34\t  R3:\n35\t    title: Differential testing\n36\t    items:\n37\t      - R3.1:\n38\t          text: Differential tests must compare stdout output and exit codes between the Go binary and the reference binary (glogname) via pkg/testutils.\n39\t      - R3.2:\n40\t          text: \"Tests must cover: normal invocation (no arguments), extra operand error, and unknown flag error.\"\n41\t      - R3.3:\n42\t          text: All differential tests must set LC_ALL=C in the environment.\n43\t\n44\tnon_goals:\n45\t  - cmd/logname does not accept a username argument.\n46\t  - cmd/logname does not print the effective username; use cmd/whoami for that.\n47\t  - cmd/logname does not print UID, GID, or group memberships; use cmd/id for that.\n48\t\n49\tacceptance_criteria:\n50\t  - id: AC1\n51\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/logname prints the login name, matching glogname.\"\n52\t    traces:\n53\t      - R1.1\n54\t      - R1.2\n55\t  - id: AC2\n56\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/logname extraarg exits 1 with an error message to stderr, matching glogname.\"\n57\t    traces:\n58\t      - R1.1\n59\t      - R2.1\n60\t      - R2.2\n61\t      - R2.3\n62\t      - R3.1\n63\t      - R3.2\n64\t  - id: AC3\n65\t    criterion: \"Differential test against glogname passes for normal invocation and error cases.\"\n66\t    traces:\n67\t      - R2.1\n68\t      - R2.2\n69\t      - R2.3\n70\t      - R3.1\n71\t      - R3.2\n72\t      - R3.3\n73\t  - id: AC4\n74\t    criterion: \"cmd/logname compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n75\t    traces:\n76\t      - R1.1\n77\t      - R1.2\n78\t      - R2.1\n79\t      - R2.2\n80\t      - R2.3\n81\t      - R3.1\n82\t      - R3.2\n83\t      - R3.3\n84\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1d52ed88-d6c0-4656-9133-eb19a12f4911","uuid":"45bc96b0-9564-48b3-a6b8-5fb1e9182d5e","timestamp":"2026-05-14T23:13:25.158Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5228/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd053-logname.yaml","content":"id: srd053-logname\ntitle: \"cmd/logname: Print Login Name\"\n\nproblem: |\n  The logname utility prints the login name of the current user as recorded by the system\n  login process. Unlike whoami (which reports the effective username), logname reports the\n  original login identity, which may differ after su or sudo. The Go implementation must\n  match the Homebrew GNU reference binary (glogname, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte\n  on stdout and exit code, verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: Print the login name of the current user followed by a newline.\n  - G2: Reject any extra operands with an error message and nonzero exit.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: Default behavior\n    items:\n      - R1.1:\n          text: When invoked with no arguments, must print the login name followed by a newline and exit 0.\n      - R1.2:\n          text: The login name must be obtained from the system login record (getlogin(3) or equivalent), not from the effective UID.\n\n  R2:\n    title: Error handling\n    items:\n      - R2.1:\n          text: If any extra operand is provided (beyond --help and --version), must print an error message to stderr and exit 1.\n      - R2.2:\n          text: Unknown flags must produce an error message to stderr and exit 1.\n      - R2.3:\n          text: If the login name cannot be determined (e.g., no controlling terminal), must print an error to stderr and exit 1.\n\n  R3:\n    title: Differential testing\n    items:\n      - R3.1:\n          text: Differential tests must compare stdout output and exit codes between the Go binary and the reference binary (glogname) via pkg/testutils.\n      - R3.2:\n          text: \"Tests must cover: normal invocation (no arguments), extra operand error, and unknown flag error.\"\n      - R3.3:\n          text: All differential tests must set LC_ALL=C in the environment.\n\nnon_goals:\n  - cmd/logname does not accept a username argument.\n  - cmd/logname does not print the effective username; use cmd/whoami for that.\n  - cmd/logname does not print UID, GID, or group memberships; use cmd/id for that.\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/logname prints the login name, matching glogname.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n  - id: AC2\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/logname extraarg exits 1 with an error message to stderr, matching glogname.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.3\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n  - id: AC3\n    criterion: \"Differential test against glogname passes for normal invocation and error cases.\"\n    traces:\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.3\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n      - R3.3\n  - id: AC4\n    criterion: \"cmd/logname compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.3\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n      - R3.3\n","numLines":84,"startLine":1,"totalLines":84}}}
